  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Ecs Federal obligated $331M in FY2026 to date across 116 awards, with an average award size of $2.9M. Ecs Federal's obligations are down 43.0% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $136M, followed by the General Services Administration with $97.4M and the Department of Justice with $47.7M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market for Ecs Federal with $159M, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $44.9M and Engineering Services at $44.6M. FY2026 to date totals are partial and reflect contract obligations rather than total contract values. Historical obligations show variability: FY21 was $494M, FY22 was $394M, FY23 was $473M, FY24 was $480M, and FY25 was $581M. These figures show where Ecs Federal's current-year revenue is concentrated by agency and by NAICS market and how current obligations compare with prior fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies buy the most from Ecs Federal?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $136M from Ecs Federal in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $97.4M and the Department of Justice obligated $47.7M. The Department of Homeland Security, Department of Commerce, and Department of the Treasury obligated $24.3M, $17.3M, and $7.4M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets drive Ecs Federal's federal work?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest NAICS market for Ecs Federal at $159M in FY2026 to date. Other Computer Related Services and Engineering Services follow with $44.9M and $44.6M respectively. Ecs Federal also shows meaningful obligations in All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $38.9M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $28.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
